Max: Hey, mom. Hey, dad. I’m back.
Max: It’s been a long time since I’ve visited, huh? Sorry, I was kind of busy.
Max: Who am I kidding? I couldn’t bring myself to come back. 
Max: If you’re here, that means I would have to accept that I would never hear from you again.
Max: It's selfish, I know. And for that, I'm sorry.
Max: I brought you guys some things from Manila. Some food, new clothes, even a bag for mom.
Max: And get this, I had a mythical pull from the ukay-ukay.
Max: THE OFFICIAL LOLO MARTIN JACKET. I know, I know, you don't have to thank me.
Max: Oh, and I also got Tita's camera. 
Max: I'm sure you guys know what it does.
Max: I tried using it at home, and it felt like I was walking in our old house again.
Max: Back in the city, Joshua and Martin begged me to take a photo of all of us. Reminded me of our parties back in college.
Max: Speaking of, I actually got these pasaluong from Tito A’s shop in Manila. 
Max: You wouldn't believe it but Joshua’s managing it now and it’s a whole lot bigger.
Max: Who knew that scrawny little boy can manage a legitimate business now.
Max: …
Max: Actually, instead of describing it, why not I just show you.
do place_photo()
Max: While I’m at it, here, take a look at this photo I took on New Year's Eve.
do place_photo()
Max: And there’s also this photo, I took during a company outing.
do place_photo()
Max: And also this time when I-
do quick_dim(2.0)
Max: ...
Max: A lot really has happened since you left. Sorry that I couldn’t come back sooner.
Max: After all that yapping I’m not too sure if you guys even got all that hahaha...
Max: …
Max: I miss you guys.
Max: I miss you guys so, so much.
Max: It's hard to get by alone. 
Max: No matter how hard I tried I can't seem to accept it.
Max: It only felt like yesterday when Mom was making sinigang for the family.
Max: ...
Max: But I know it's selfish to be stuck in the past.
Max: You guys would want to see me live the life I wanted, even if it's without you.
Max: And for that and that alone, I will crawl my way through this world, inch by inch.
Max: Thank you for everything. I love you guys.
Max: The next time I come back, I’m going to bring a lot more photos to show. I promise.
Max: Until then.
